ow to export each report as CSV.\n- Published documentation explains safe reclamation steps and clearly states\n  that no automated reclamation or deletion is performed by the platform.\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports so\n  that described columns, thresholds, and behavior match what ships.\n- Documentation is delivered through the Red Hat docs content process.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps —\n  fully covered by this epic. Substantive content authoring is a distinct work\n  stream from the code implementation, which is why this is a separate\n  docs-authoring epic rather than scope on the report epics.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32744,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-867557591d0cc8ac","agent_id":"ac5ab4f93e9ccb280","session_id":"0a069a60-d094-4d49-bf51-a08d3019870c","uuid":"bb538132-3179-4bff-99cc-627642c679bd","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:16:08.674Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
