{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd25c79cc0d56b97","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9016 (Idle resource reporting in the web console)\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). Although the strategy is\n15\tsmall and the console work itself would score high on AI implementability, the\n16\tscope spans multiple distinct work streams — console code implementation plus\n17\tsubstantive documentation authoring (HLR-4: new doc topics explaining the reports\n18\tand safe reclamation steps) — and touches multiple platform components. The\n19\tmultiple-work-stream escape condition applies, so the strategy proceeds through\n20\tthe full decomposition.\n21\t\n22\t## Component Graph\n23\t\n24\tCanonical component mapping (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`):\n25\t\n26\t| Strategy component | Canonical name | Classification | Handling |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | Active (code changes) | Generates implementation epics |\n29\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Passive (no code changes — data already tracked) | Validation AC on the workbench-report epic |\n30\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | Passive (no code changes — run metadata already retained) | Validation AC on the pipeline-run-report epic |\n31\t\n32\tMapping notes (non-obvious): \"RHOAI web console\" maps to the canonical\n33\t`Dashboard` component; \"Notebook controller\" maps to `Notebooks`;\n34\t\"Kubeflow Pipelines\" maps to `Data Science Pipelines`. Both passive components\n35\tare corroborated by architecture context (`.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/notebooks.md`\n36\tconfirms last-activity tracking via the culler's per-kernel Jupyter server API\n37\tprobes; `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/data-science-pipelines.md`\n38\tconfirms KFP v2 run metadata and that pipeline runs are already surfaced in the\n39\tDashboard). The strategy states \"the data exists; it is just not surfaced\n40\tanywhere\", so no code changes are planned in the passive components. Validation\n41\tthat each report faithfully reflects the upstream data source is an acceptance\n42\tcriterion on the corresponding Dashboard epic; the strategy assigns no\n43\tcross-team validation work, so no separate validation epics are generated.\n44\t\n45\tAll three components exist in architecture context — no new-component\n46\tonboarding chain is needed; the Dashboard is already Konflux-onboarded.\n47\t\n48\t## Epic List\n49\t\n50\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n51\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Stale pipeline-run report in the web console | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E003 | Documentation for the idle resource reports and safe reclamation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Documentation | P2 |\n55\t\n56\t## Dependency DAG\n57\t\n58\t```mermaid\n59\tgraph TD\n60\t    E001[\"E001: Idle-workbench report (Dashboard, P1)\"]\n61\t    E002[\"E002: Stale pipeline-run report (Dashboard, P1)\"]\n62\t    E003[\"E003: Report documentation (docs-authoring, P2)\"]\n63\t    E001 --> E003\n64\t    E002 --> E003\n65\t```\n66\t\n67\t## DAG Justification\n68\t\n69\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n70\t|---|---|---|\n71\t| E001 ∥ E002 (no edge) | Rule 15 | Same repo (Dashboard), different areas: the workbench report sources from notebook-controller activity data while the pipeline-run report sources from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata. Distinct data integrations and distinct report surfaces; neither builds against an artifact the other