er priority: Normal → P2). |\n83\t\n84\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n85\t\n86\t## Health Warnings\n87\t\n88\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy provides HLRs, an affected-component\n89\t  list, out-of-scope items, and an explicit \"Open Questions: None\", but omits the\n90\t  detailed Affected Components table (per-component change/owner), the Impacted\n91\t  Teams table, the Dependencies table, Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, NFRs,\n92\t  and an effort estimate. Epic acceptance criteria were derived from the HLRs;\n93\t  team ownership for the implementation epics comes from the architecture-context\n94\t  owning team for `Dashboard` (RHOAI Dashboard). The docs epic's owning team\n95\t  (\"RHOAI Documentation\") is inferred from the Red Hat docs content process —\n96\t  planners should confirm the actual docs owner.\n97\t- **Data-access assumption (scope note)**: HLR-1 presumes the notebook\n98\t  controller's last-activity data is readable by the console. Architecture\n99\t  context confirms activity tracking exists (per-kernel Jupyter server API\n100\t  probes used by the idle culler), and the strategy asserts the data exists and\n101\t  needs only surfacing, with no open questions. If implementation finds the\n102\t  activity data is not exposed in a form the console can read (for example, not\n103\t  published on the Notebook CR status), follow-up work in the `Notebooks`\n104\t  component (Workbenches team) would be required and should be scoped then.\n105\t  Recorded here for planner awareness; not an Investigation epic because the\n106\t  strategy author explicitly resolved the question (\"the data exists\").\n107\t- **Out-of-scope guard**: automated reclamation/deletion and cost/chargeback are\n108\t  explicitly out of scope; report epics carry ACs that no reclamation/deletion\n109\t  actions are offered, so the reports cannot imply capability the platform does\n110\t  not provide.\n111\t\n112\t## Tiered Delivery\n113\t\n114\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; both data\n115\tsources are in-platform and generally available per architecture context.\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00bd1bb76f169d7","agent_id":"a56077b4d755d6c97","session_id":"0a069a60-d094-4d49-bf51-a08d3019870c","uuid":"676c566e-753d-4f5d-9e50-7e0b9ba9b6f1","timestamp":"2026-10-25T20:17:35.581Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd25c79cc0d56b97","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
