{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81f360afa59b1215","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Per-project idle-workbench report in the web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers a per-project idle-workbench report in the RHOAI web\n34\tconsole. Cluster administrators can see, for each data science project, which\n35\tworkbenches are sitting idle: each entry shows the workbench's last activity,\n36\tits owner, and its reserved resources. The report is sourced from the notebook\n37\tcontroller's existing activity tracking — no changes to the notebook controller\n38\titself; its data is surfaced for the first time. The report also supports CSV\n39\texport so administrators can take the data elsewhere.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A new report surface in the web console, scoped per project, listing idle\n44\t  workbenches.\n45\t- Report columns: workbench name, last activity (from the notebook controller's\n46\t  activity tracking), owner, and reserved resources (the workbench's resource\n47\t  reservations and attached storage).\n48\t- Data sourcing from the notebook controller's activity tracking; the mechanism\n49\t  by which the console reads that data (e.g. from the workbench's status or\n50\t  another readable source) is an implementation decision for the Dashboard team.\n51\t- Idle classification based on last-activity age; the specific idle threshold\n52\t  used for the report is an implementation decision.\n53\t- CSV export of the workbench report, including the displayed rows and columns.\n54\t- Empty-state handling for projects with no idle workbenches.\n55\t- No reclamation, deletion, or other mutating actions on workbenches from the\n56\t  report (automated reclamation is out of scope for the strategy).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a project containing workbenches with varying recent activity, the\n61\t  report lists each idle workbench with its last-activity time, owner, and\n62\t  reserved resources.\n63\t- Given a project with no idle workbenches, the report shows an empty state\n64\t  rather than an error.\n65\t- The last-activity values shown in the report match the notebook controller's\n66\t  activity tracking for the same workbenches (validation of the Notebooks\n67\t  component as a passive data source).\n68\t- An administrator can export the workbench report as CSV, and the exported\n69\t  file contains the rows and columns displayed in the console.\n70\t- The report offers no action that stops, deletes, or otherwise mutates a\n71\t  workbench — reporting only.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner,\n76\t  reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity\n77\t  tracking — fully covered by this epic.\n78\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of this report is included here rather than\n79\t  a separate epic — the export edits the same report surface this epic builds,\n80\t  so splitting would double-touch the same components.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00bd1bb76f169d7","agent_id":"a56077b4d755d6c97","session_id":"0a069a60-d094-4d49-bf51-a08d3019870c","uuid":"8d945ace-b692-47c